  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that the President, using express statutory authority, made terrorism\u2011related provisions inapplicable to Iraq, removing those provisions of law that previously applied to countries sponsoring terrorism."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, they further contend that because section 1605(a)(7) was rendered inapplicable to Iraq, it cannot serve as a basis for abrogating Iraq\u2019s foreign sovereign immunity or establishing subject\u2011matter jurisdiction."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 16,
              "start": 16
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States (amicus curiae), the United States, as amicus curiae, maintains that the President\u2019s authority under EWSAA section\u202f1503 to make such provisions inapplicable to Iraq is clear and entitled to deference."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Plaintiffs argue that despite the removal of terrorism\u2011sponsor status, they are not left without any remedy and should be treated like other claimants against a foreign state."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
