              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, the President, acting with express statutory authority, made terrorism\u2011related provisions inapplicable to Iraq, removing those provisions of law that applied to countries that sponsored terrorism."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners, because section\u202f1605(a)(7) was made inapplicable to Iraq, it cannot serve as the statutory basis for abrogating Iraq\u2019s foreign sovereign immunity or establishing subject\u2011matter jurisdiction."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner: Republic of Iraq",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
          "citations": [
