              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Plaintiffs argue that they are not left without any remedy; they should be treated like any other claimant against a foreign state that is not on the small list of designated state sponsors of terrorism."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 38
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Mr. Goldstein argues that the word \u201cany\u201d in the statute means \u201cevery,\u201d supporting a broad application of the law."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 41,
                "start": 41
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Goldstein, he cites cases such as Atascadero and Raygor to illustrate that \u201cany\u201d means \u201cevery\u201d except for the states."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "4a3fc18f745c662985bcf5ad83f5aad978c9da9eed53ed106067e5daf58caf66",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-4a3fc18f745c-0002-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 45,
                "start": 45
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Goldstein, he notes that the Solicitor General is correct that these claims, pleaded as state\u2011law claims, provide a substantive cause of action."
        }
